 ## Lifetime
 
-Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
+Each request renews the session for 30 minutes; [larder/sessions.py](../../larder/sessions.py) defines the expiry
+and the signing and verification functions. Until March 2024 the limit
 was 10 minutes: members packing a pantry order on a slow mobile connection were logged out before they confirmed it
 and lost what they had picked, and support logged 120 tickets about it that month. The limit was raised to 30
 minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The [signed-cookie decision](../adrs/0001-use-signed-session-cookies.md) explains the storage choice and why it
+replaced Postgres. The cookie carries the member and expiry with a signature; its contents are not encrypted.
+
+## Configuration
+
+`LARDER_SESSION_KEY` supplies the shared signing key through the deploy secrets. Every web server must use the
+same value. [larder/sessions.py](../../larder/sessions.py) reads it at module import and falls back to `dev-only`
+when it is absent; deployments must supply the secret.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A member's session cannot be revoked individually from the server before it expires. Wait for the
+  [session lifetime](#lifetime), or rotate the shared key if everyone must be logged out.
+- Rotating the key logs everyone out. Rotate it only between pickups, as agreed in
+  [issue 63](../../notes/issue-63.md), and have all web servers load the new value.
 
